  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @brief Convolution of Q7 sequences.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length srcALen+src
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in]  *pScratch1 points to scratch buffer(of type q15_t) of size max(srcALen, srcBLen) + 2
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @param[in]  *pScratch2 points to scratch buffer (of type q15_t) of size min(srcALen, srcBLen).
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * \par Restrictions
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *  If the silicon does not support unaligned memory access enable the macro UNALIGNED_SUPPORT_DISA
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *	In this case input, output, scratch1 and scratch2 buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * @details
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * \par
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 32-bit internal accumulator.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * Both the inputs are represented in 1.7 format and multiplications yield a 2.14 result.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * The 2.14 intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit accumulator in 18.14 format.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * This approach provides 17 guard bits and there is no risk of overflow as long as <code>max(srcAL
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  * The 18.14 result is then truncated to 18.7 format by discarding the low 7 bits and then saturate
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_opt_q7.c ****  */
